#!/usr/bin/env -S m9c --run
MODULE ListDiff ;

(* listdiff -- the hand-maintained module lists must agree.

       runtime/test/ListDiff.m9

   A corpus module is named in several places by hand, and until this
   gate nothing checked that they said the same thing.  Every drift so
   far was found by something else failing later:

     2026-08-24  gentest.pas, gendiff.sh, bootstrap.sh, build.sh
                 LIBRARY, m9c.sh -- "every one was found by something
                 failing"
     2026-08-29  Mat gained a Math import; bootstrap.sh's deps_of did
                 not, and stage2 broke
     2026-09-11  ApiSpec, Arrow, Delim, Zip and Zarr joined
                 gentest.pas and not gendiff.sh or bootstrap.sh; Http
                 gained an Io import in gentest alone.  CI never saw it
                 because the lexer golden was stale too and every later
                 job waits on that one.

   What is checked, each rule stated with the reason it is the rule:

     1. gentest.pas, gendiff.sh and bootstrap.sh name the SAME modules
        with the SAME dependency lists, in the same order.  gendiff.sh's
        own header says "the dep lists must match gentest.pas exactly";
        bootstrap.sh emits every module from every stage with those
        deps.  (LibmGate and the other gendiff fixtures are excluded.)

     2. Every module in corpus/ is in gentest.pas, except the ones in
        NotGenerated with a reason each.  A module the FPC generator
        never sees is a module runtime/gen does not hold and the
        bootstrap cannot build.

     3. A module's DIRECT imports are a subset of its gentest deps, and
        every dep is inside the module's import CLOSURE.  The deps are
        what LoadExtern registers and what the generator #includes: an
        import missing from them is an unknown callee (the 2026-09-11
        failure), and a dep the module can never reach is a dead
        include (Sem carried Fmt, Fmt carried DynStr, neither used --
        removed the same day).  Not equality with either the direct
        set or the closure: some lists carry the closure and some the
        direct imports, and changing one moves the emitted #includes.
        A dep outside the closure is refused.  There was one excuse,
        by name with its reason: HttpServer named Http because `FROM
        csock IMPORT` needs the foreign unit declared in Http.m9.  It
        ended on 2026-10-06, when HttpServer began importing Http for
        Http.Header; the excuse was then refused as stale, and the
        mechanism went with it (an empty constant table has no type).

     4. build.sh's LIBRARY is every corpus module except those named in
        NotInstalled with a reason each.  That list is what docgen and
        docdiff iterate and what the package installs to /usr/lib/m9.

     5. tools/tutor/setup.sh's LIB is a subset of LIBRARY and is closed
        under direct imports: a cell that compiles against a hermetic
        copy of the library cannot reach a module that is not in it.

     6. build.sh's COMPILER is closed under direct imports, for the
        same reason at link time.

     7. m9c.sh's `check M deps...` lines carry gentest.pas's deps for
        M.  They compile M with NAMED deps and compare the bytes with
        the oracle's, and named deps win, so a stale line there emits
        an #include the oracle does not and the gate diverges for a
        reason that is not the compiler's.

     8. Every gate that links an m9c of its own (`... -o m9c` or
        `-o "$W/m9c"` in runtime/test/*.sh) links exactly build.sh's
        COMPILER modules.  Twelve scripts carry that line by hand; ten
        still linked Fmt.c and three Time.c after nothing in the
        compiler imported either (2026-09-11) -- dead under LTO, but a
        module MISSING from one of them is a link error only that gate
        sees.

     9. Every battery in runtime/test/build.sh links a set of generated
        modules that is CLOSED under direct imports.  The driver lines
        name their `../gen/M.c` by hand -- the script's own comment
        counts three times one of them missed Json -- and a missing one
        is a link error in one battery of thirty-eight; here it is one
        line naming the module and the import.

    10. Every module gentest.pas generates is linked by at least one
        battery of build.sh, or is named in NoBattery with what holds
        it instead.  A library module that lands without a driver is a
        module nothing runs.

    11. The tutorial has NO hand link line (runtime/test/lib/
        tutcommon.sh): since 2026-10-09 every example links flagless,
        the FOR "C" units naming their libraries (LINK, par 7).  Until
        then five examples had a gcc line each, held closed under
        imports by this rule -- when Stats gained Bits on 2026-09-27
        only tutgen failing to link C14Flux said so -- and a line
        that comes back is a library the compiler does not know to
        link, which is the compiler's gap, not the gate's.

    12. The link lines of every OTHER gate over runtime/gen, and
        bootstrap.sh's TOOLC, are closed under direct imports as rule
        9 holds build.sh's.  When Gen gained Text on 2026-10-01 the
        first three rules named gentest, gendiff's run line and
        deps_of; the helper both gendiff and bootstrap LINK was left to
        the linker, once in each gate, the second after a ten-minute
        run.

    13. corpus/NAMETest.m9 is the test of corpus/NAME.m9 (m9test.sh
        builds and runs it): excused from gentest and from LIBRARY by
        its name, so the name must have a module behind it.

   Exit status 1 with every disagreement named; 0 when all agree.

   It replaced runtime/test/listdiff.py on 2026-10-04, after the two
   printed the same lines over the tree and over every sabotage the
   gate's history names.  The messages are the Python's, list syntax
   and all, so a reader of old logs reads the new ones the same way.
   Each regular expression the Python used is here as a few lines of
   scanning, with the rule it kept: an IMPORT line is matched at its
   start and read to its FIRST semicolon; a word is [A-Za-z0-9_]; a
   backslash at a line's end joins the next line; files are octets. *)

IMPORT Io ;
IMPORT Text ;
IMPORT DynStr ;
IMPORT Fmt ;
IMPORT Sort ;

CONST
  Room = 256 ;                 (* the most names one set holds *)

  (* a corpus module gentest.pas deliberately does not generate *)
  NotGenerated = ['LibmGate', 'KindUse', 'EnumUse', 'Palette', 'Lsp',
                  'M9fmt', 'M9elide'] ;
  NotGeneratedWhy = ['gendiff-only fixture (96 libm-named locals)',
                     'gendiff-only fixture (a case record used across a module)',
                     'gendiff-only fixture (an enumeration used across a module)',
                     'gendiff-only fixture (an enumeration declaration)',
                     'program module built by m9c --make from the library',
                     'program module built by m9c --make from the library',
                     'program module built by m9c --make from the library'] ;
  (* a corpus module build.sh deliberately does not install *)
  NotInstalled = ['LibmGate', 'KindUse', 'EnumUse', 'Palette', 'Hello',
                  'Concat', 'Narrow', 'ProcUse', 'AggUse', 'ShareUse',
                  'ExportDef', 'ExportUse', 'M9c'] ;
  NotInstalledWhy = ['gendiff-only fixture', 'gendiff-only fixture',
                     'gendiff-only fixture', 'gendiff-only fixture',
                     'demo program',
                     'demo program (the executable half of the + decision)',
                     'test program (every integer width traps on overflow)',
                     'test program (procedure types, par 2.2.3)',
                     'test program (constant tables, par 2.2.4)',
                     'test program (a call that raised answered nothing, par 5)',
                     'test fixture (exported module variables, decision 28)',
                     'test program (exported module variables, decision 28)',
                     'the compiler itself, installed as a binary'] ;
  (* a generated module no battery of runtime/test/build.sh links, and
     the gate that holds it instead *)
  NoBattery = ['Lex', 'Ast', 'Parse', 'Print', 'Sem', 'Gen', 'Doc', 'Diag',
               'M9c', 'Review', 'Check', 'Arrays', 'Numeric', 'Png', 'NbCells',
               'NbShow', 'ExportDef', 'ExportUse', 'Pg', 'Sparql', 'Rdf', 'Regex', 'Xml', 'Hash', 'Smtp', 'Rsa', 'Map',
               'Parquet'] ;
  NoBatteryWhy = ['lexdiff, comdiff and the token-count golden',
                  'parsediff (every node kind printed back)',
                  'parsediff and the parse probes',
                  'parsediff (print (parse ()) is the fixpoint)',
                  'semdiff and probediff',
                  'gendiff and bootstrap',
                  'docdiff',
                  'diagdiff and the tutor gate',
                  'm9c.sh, the compiler as a program',
                  'reviewdiff (one recorded page per corpus module)',
                  'm9test (CheckTest holds it to its own recorded output)',
                  'm9test (ArraysTest, against numpy goldens)',
                  'm9test (NumericTest, against scipy goldens)',
                  'm9test (PngTest, read back through Zip.Decompress) and deflate.sh (Python reads the files)',
                  'm9test (NbCellsTest, every kind back to the bit) and jupyter.sh (the kernel hands a value between cells)',
                  'm9test (NbShowTest, every form to its text) and jupyter.sh (an expression cell shows its value)',
                  'gendiff and run.sh (ExportUse writes, ExportDef reads the same storage)',
                  'gendiff and run.sh (ExportUse writes, ExportDef reads the same storage)',
                  'm9test (PgTest against a Postgres server, psycopg goldens; CI runs one)',
                  'm9test (SparqlTest offline, rdflib goldens) and sparql.sh (live, rdflib serving)',
                  'm9test (RdfTest over the W3C suites) and rdf.sh (rdflib judges the graphs)',
                  'm9test (RegexTest, against Python re goldens)',
                  'xml.sh (XmlTest over the W3C conformance suite, fetched) and m9test (the cases by hand)',
                  'm9test (HashTest, against hashlib goldens)',
                  'smtp.sh (SmtpFix against aiosmtpd, judged by Python email) and m9test (SmtpTest, the message against goldens)',
                  'm9test (RsaTest, against signatures and forgeries from Python cryptography)',
                  'm9test (MapTest, against pyproj, numpy and the Natural Earth file)',
                  "m9test (ParquetTest, pyarrow's files against what pyarrow reads) and columnar.sh (pyarrow reads what the writer wrote)"] ;
  GendiffFixtures = ['LibmGate', 'KindUse', 'EnumUse', 'Palette'] ;

TYPE
  (* a set of names, kept in insertion order: Python's dicts and the
     lists it printed were ordered, and the messages follow that order *)
  Names = RECORD
    n : I64 ;
    v : SLICE OF STR ;
  END ;
  Entry = RECORD
    name : STR ;
    deps : Names ;
  END ;

VAR
  pool : POOL ;
  root : STR ;
  bad : Names ;                (* the disagreements, in order *)
  corpus : Names ;
  impName : SLICE OF STR ;     (* corpus module i ... *)
  impSet : SLICE OF Names ;    (* ... and its direct imports *)
  gt, gd, bs : SLICE OF Entry ;
  notGen, notInst : Names ;    (* the excuses, rule 13's added *)

(* ---- sets of names ---- *)

PROCEDURE Fresh () : Names =
VAR s : Names ;
BEGIN
  s.n := 0 ;
  s.v := NEW (pool, STR, Room) ;
  RETURN s
END Fresh ;

PROCEDURE Has (RO s: Names ; RO x: STR) : BOOL =
VAR i : I64 ;
BEGIN
  FOR i := 0 TO s.n - 1 DO
    IF DynStr.Eq (s.v[i], x) THEN RETURN TRUE END
  END ;
  RETURN FALSE
END Has ;

PROCEDURE HasIn (RO a: SLICE OF STR ; RO x: STR) : BOOL =
VAR i : I64 ;
BEGIN
  FOR i := 0 TO LEN (a) - 1 DO
    IF DynStr.Eq (a[i], x) THEN RETURN TRUE END
  END ;
  RETURN FALSE
END HasIn ;

(* x at the end, a copy in the program's pool; a set keeps one of each *)
PROCEDURE Add (VAR s: Names ; RO x: STR) =
BEGIN
  IF NOT Has (s, x) THEN
    s.v[s.n] := Text.Keep (pool, x) ;
    s.n := s.n + 1
  END
END Add ;

(* the same, duplicates kept: a list, as gentest's deps are *)
PROCEDURE Push (VAR s: Names ; RO x: STR) =
BEGIN
  s.v[s.n] := Text.Keep (pool, x) ;
  s.n := s.n + 1
END Push ;

PROCEDURE FromTable (RO a: SLICE OF STR) : Names =
VAR
  s : Names ;
  i : I64 ;
BEGIN
  s := Fresh () ;
  FOR i := 0 TO LEN (a) - 1 DO Push (s, a[i]) END ;
  RETURN s
END FromTable ;

(* a's names that are not in b, sorted -- Python's sorted (a - b) *)
PROCEDURE Minus (RO a, b: Names) : Names =
VAR
  s : Names ;
  i : I64 ;
BEGIN
  s := Fresh () ;
  FOR i := 0 TO a.n - 1 DO
    IF NOT Has (b, a.v[i]) THEN Add (s, a.v[i]) END
  END ;
  Sorted (s) ;
  RETURN s
END Minus ;

PROCEDURE Sorted (VAR s: Names) =
VAR
  w : SLICE OF STR ;
  i : I64 ;
BEGIN
  w := NEW (pool, STR, s.n) ;
  FOR i := 0 TO s.n - 1 DO w[i] := s.v[i] END ;
  Sort.Strs (w) ;
  FOR i := 0 TO s.n - 1 DO s.v[i] := w[i] END
END Sorted ;

PROCEDURE SameSet (RO a, b: Names) : BOOL =
VAR i : I64 ;
BEGIN
  FOR i := 0 TO a.n - 1 DO
    IF NOT Has (b, a.v[i]) THEN RETURN FALSE END
  END ;
  FOR i := 0 TO b.n - 1 DO
    IF NOT Has (a, b.v[i]) THEN RETURN FALSE END
  END ;
  RETURN TRUE
END SameSet ;

PROCEDURE SameList (RO a, b: Names) : BOOL =
VAR i : I64 ;
BEGIN
  IF a.n # b.n THEN RETURN FALSE END ;
  FOR i := 0 TO a.n - 1 DO
    IF NOT DynStr.Eq (a.v[i], b.v[i]) THEN RETURN FALSE END
  END ;
  RETURN TRUE
END SameList ;

(* a list as Python's str () prints one: ['A', 'B'] *)
PROCEDURE Repr (RO s: Names) : STR =
VAR
  d : PTR DynStr.DString IN pool ;
  i : I64 ;
BEGIN
  d := DynStr.New (pool) ;
  DynStr.AppendChar (d, '[') ;
  FOR i := 0 TO s.n - 1 DO
    IF i > 0 THEN DynStr.Append (d, ', ') END ;
    DynStr.Append (d, "'") ;
    DynStr.Append (d, s.v[i]) ;
    DynStr.Append (d, "'")
  END ;
  DynStr.AppendChar (d, ']') ;
  RETURN DynStr.View (d)
END Repr ;

PROCEDURE Fail (RO msg: STR) =
BEGIN
  Push (bad, msg)
END Fail ;

(* ---- reading ---- *)

PROCEDURE Rd (RO path: STR) : STR RAISES Io.IOError, ValueRange =
BEGIN
  RETURN DynStr.Chars (pool, Io.ReadFileBytes (pool, root + '/' + path))
END Rd ;

(* the text with every backslash-newline replaced by a blank *)
PROCEDURE Joined (RO s: STR) : STR =
VAR
  d : PTR DynStr.DString IN pool ;
  i : I64 ;
BEGIN
  d := DynStr.New (pool) ;
  i := 0 ;
  WHILE i < LEN (s) DO
    IF (s[i] = 05CC) AND (i + 1 < LEN (s)) AND (s[i + 1] = 0AC) THEN
      DynStr.AppendChar (d, ' ') ;
      i := i + 2
    ELSE
      DynStr.AppendChar (d, s[i]) ;
      i := i + 1
    END
  END ;
  RETURN DynStr.View (d)
END Joined ;

PROCEDURE IsWord (c: CHAR) : BOOL =
BEGIN
  RETURN ((c >= 'a') AND (c <= 'z')) OR ((c >= 'A') AND (c <= 'Z')) OR
         ((c >= '0') AND (c <= '9')) OR (c = '_')
END IsWord ;

PROCEDURE IsBlank (c: CHAR) : BOOL =
BEGIN
  RETURN (c = ' ') OR (c = 09C) OR (c = 0AC) OR (c = 0DC) OR
         (c = 0BC) OR (c = 0CC)
END IsBlank ;

(* the blank-separated words of s, Python's split () *)
PROCEDURE Words (RO s: STR) : Names =
VAR
  w : Names ;
  i, j : I64 ;
BEGIN
  w := Fresh () ;
  i := 0 ;
  WHILE i < LEN (s) DO
    WHILE (i < LEN (s)) AND IsBlank (s[i]) DO i := i + 1 END ;
    j := i ;
    WHILE (j < LEN (s)) AND NOT IsBlank (s[j]) DO j := j + 1 END ;
    IF j > i THEN Push (w, SLICE (s, i, j - i)) END ;
    i := j
  END ;
  RETURN w
END Words ;

(* s without blanks at either end *)
PROCEDURE Strip (RO s: STR) : STR =
VAR a, b : I64 ;
BEGIN
  a := 0 ;
  b := LEN (s) ;
  WHILE (a < b) AND IsBlank (s[a]) DO a := a + 1 END ;
  WHILE (b > a) AND IsBlank (s[b - 1]) DO b := b - 1 END ;
  RETURN SLICE (s, a, b - a)
END Strip ;

(* the source with every comment blanked, nesting honoured and the
   line breaks kept.  Check.m9's documentation shows a test, IMPORT
   line and all, and was read as importing itself. *)
PROCEDURE NoComments (RO s: STR) : STR =
VAR
  d : PTR DynStr.DString IN pool ;
  i, depth : I64 ;
BEGIN
  d := DynStr.New (pool) ;
  depth := 0 ;
  i := 0 ;
  WHILE i < LEN (s) DO
    IF (s[i] = '(') AND (i + 1 < LEN (s)) AND (s[i + 1] = '*') THEN
      depth := depth + 1 ;
      i := i + 2
    ELSIF (depth > 0) AND (s[i] = '*') AND (i + 1 < LEN (s)) AND (s[i + 1] = ')') THEN
      depth := depth - 1 ;
      i := i + 2
    ELSE
      IF (depth = 0) OR (s[i] = 0AC) THEN DynStr.AppendChar (d, s[i]) END ;
      i := i + 1
    END
  END ;
  RETURN DynStr.View (d)
END NoComments ;

(* the names of an IMPORT line, added to s: the line's start, blanks,
   IMPORT, at least one blank, then everything to the FIRST semicolon,
   split at commas.  FROM u IMPORT is a foreign unit and does not
   match. *)
PROCEDURE ImportLine (RO line: STR ; VAR s: Names) =
VAR
  i, j, k : I64 ;
  part : SLICE OF STR ;
BEGIN
  i := 0 ;
  WHILE (i < LEN (line)) AND IsBlank (line[i]) DO i := i + 1 END ;
  IF (LEN (line) - i < 7) OR NOT Text.Eq (SLICE (line, i, 6), 'IMPORT') THEN RETURN END ;
  IF NOT IsBlank (line[i + 6]) THEN RETURN END ;
  j := i + 6 ;
  k := Text.FindChar (SLICE (line, j, LEN (line) - j), ';') ;
  IF k < 0 THEN RETURN END ;
  part := Text.Split (SLICE (line, j, k), ',') ;
  FOR k := 0 TO LEN (part) - 1 DO
    IF LEN (Strip (part[k])) > 0 THEN Add (s, Strip (part[k])) END
  END
END ImportLine ;

(* the direct imports of corpus module m; the empty set for a name
   that is not one *)
PROCEDURE Direct (RO m: STR) : Names =
VAR i : I64 ;
BEGIN
  FOR i := 0 TO LEN (impName) - 1 DO
    IF DynStr.Eq (impName[i], m) THEN RETURN impSet[i] END
  END ;
  RETURN Fresh ()
END Direct ;

PROCEDURE ReadImports () RAISES Io.IOError, ValueRange =
VAR
  i, k : I64 ;
  lines : SLICE OF STR ;
  s : Names ;
BEGIN
  impName := NEW (pool, STR, corpus.n) ;
  impSet := NEW (pool, Names, corpus.n) ;
  FOR i := 0 TO corpus.n - 1 DO
    s := Fresh () ;
    lines := Text.Split (NoComments (Rd ('corpus/' + corpus.v[i] + '.m9')), 0AC) ;
    FOR k := 0 TO LEN (lines) - 1 DO ImportLine (lines[k], s) END ;
    impName[i] := corpus.v[i] ;
    impSet[i] := s
  END
END ReadImports ;

(* every name m imports, directly or through another corpus module *)
PROCEDURE Close (RO m: STR ; VAR seen: Names) =
VAR
  d : Names ;
  i : I64 ;
BEGIN
  IF NOT Has (corpus, m) THEN RETURN END ;
  d := Direct (m) ;
  FOR i := 0 TO d.n - 1 DO
    IF NOT Has (seen, d.v[i]) THEN
      Add (seen, d.v[i]) ;
      Close (d.v[i], seen)
    END
  END
END Close ;

PROCEDURE Closure (RO m: STR) : Names =
VAR s : Names ;
BEGIN
  s := Fresh () ;
  Close (m, s) ;
  RETURN s
END Closure ;

(* ---- the three generator lists ---- *)

PROCEDURE Find (RO t: SLICE OF Entry ; n: I64 ; RO m: STR) : I64 =
VAR i : I64 ;
BEGIN
  FOR i := 0 TO n - 1 DO
    IF DynStr.Eq (t[i].name, m) THEN RETURN i END
  END ;
  RETURN -1
END Find ;

PROCEDURE Shrink (RO KEPT t: SLICE OF Entry ; n: I64) : SLICE OF Entry =
VAR
  r : SLICE OF Entry ;
  i : I64 ;
BEGIN
  r := NEW (pool, Entry, n) ;
  FOR i := 0 TO n - 1 DO r[i] := t[i] END ;
  RETURN r
END Shrink ;

(* GenModule ('M', ['A', 'B']) lines of gentest.pas; a name seen twice
   keeps its first place and its last list, as a dict did *)
PROCEDURE Gentest () : SLICE OF Entry RAISES Io.IOError, ValueRange =
VAR
  s, body : STR ;
  t : SLICE OF Entry ;
  n, p, i, j, k, at : I64 ;
  part : SLICE OF STR ;
  deps : Names ;
  x : STR ;
BEGIN
  s := Rd ('host/fpc/gentest.pas') ;
  t := NEW (pool, Entry, Room) ;
  n := 0 ;
  p := 0 ;
  LOOP
    k := Text.Find (SLICE (s, p, LEN (s) - p), "GenModule ('") ;
    IF k < 0 THEN EXIT END ;
    i := p + k + 12 ;
    j := i ;
    WHILE (j < LEN (s)) AND IsWord (s[j]) DO j := j + 1 END ;
    IF (j > i) AND (j + 4 <= LEN (s)) AND Text.Eq (SLICE (s, j, 4), "', [") THEN
      k := Text.FindChar (SLICE (s, j + 4, LEN (s) - j - 4), ']') ;
      IF k >= 0 THEN
        body := SLICE (s, j + 4, k) ;
        deps := Fresh () ;
        part := Text.Split (body, ',') ;
        FOR k := 0 TO LEN (part) - 1 DO
          IF LEN (Strip (part[k])) > 0 THEN
            x := part[k] ;
            WHILE (LEN (x) > 0) AND ((x[0] = "'") OR (x[0] = ' ')) DO
              x := SLICE (x, 1, LEN (x) - 1)
            END ;
            WHILE (LEN (x) > 0) AND ((x[LEN (x) - 1] = "'") OR (x[LEN (x) - 1] = ' ')) DO
              x := SLICE (x, 0, LEN (x) - 1)
            END ;
            Push (deps, x)
          END
        END ;
        at := Find (t, n, SLICE (s, i, j - i)) ;
        IF at < 0 THEN
          t[n].name := Text.Keep (pool, SLICE (s, i, j - i)) ;
          t[n].deps := deps ;
          n := n + 1
        ELSE
          t[at].deps := deps
        END
      END
    END ;
    p := i
  END ;
  RETURN Shrink (t, n)
END Gentest ;

(* a line of the form `KEYWORD M dep dep ...`, blanks between, nothing
   else on it: gendiff.sh's run lines and m9c.sh's check lines *)
PROCEDURE ListLine (RO line, keyword: STR ; VAR m: STR ; VAR deps: Names) : BOOL =
VAR
  w : Names ;
  i, k : I64 ;
BEGIN
  IF (LEN (line) <= LEN (keyword)) OR NOT Text.StartsWith (line, keyword) THEN
    RETURN FALSE
  END ;
  IF NOT IsBlank (line[LEN (keyword)]) THEN RETURN FALSE END ;
  w := Words (SLICE (line, LEN (keyword), LEN (line) - LEN (keyword))) ;
  IF w.n = 0 THEN RETURN FALSE END ;
  FOR i := 0 TO w.n - 1 DO
    FOR k := 0 TO LEN (w.v[i]) - 1 DO
      IF NOT IsWord (w.v[i][k]) THEN RETURN FALSE END
    END
  END ;
  m := w.v[0] ;
  deps := Fresh () ;
  FOR i := 1 TO w.n - 1 DO Push (deps, w.v[i]) END ;
  RETURN TRUE
END ListLine ;

PROCEDURE Gendiff () : SLICE OF Entry RAISES Io.IOError, ValueRange =
VAR
  lines : SLICE OF STR ;
  t : SLICE OF Entry ;
  n, i, at : I64 ;
  m : STR ;
  deps : Names ;
BEGIN
  lines := Text.Split (Rd ('runtime/test/gendiff.sh'), 0AC) ;
  t := NEW (pool, Entry, Room) ;
  n := 0 ;
  FOR i := 0 TO LEN (lines) - 1 DO
    IF ListLine (lines[i], 'run', m, deps) THEN
      IF NOT HasIn (GendiffFixtures, m) THEN
        at := Find (t, n, m) ;
        IF at < 0 THEN
          t[n].name := m ; t[n].deps := deps ; n := n + 1
        ELSE
          t[at].deps := deps
        END
      END
    END
  END ;
  RETURN Shrink (t, n)
END Gendiff ;

(* NAME="..." at the start of a line, the value to the next quote,
   its backslash-newlines read as blanks, split at blanks *)
PROCEDURE ShellList (RO text, name: STR) : Names =
VAR
  lines : SLICE OF STR ;
  i, k, start : I64 ;
  head : STR ;
BEGIN
  head := Text.Keep (pool, name + '="') ;
  start := -1 ;
  IF Text.StartsWith (text, head) THEN start := LEN (head) END ;
  IF start < 0 THEN
    k := Text.Find (text, '' + 0AC + head) ;
    IF k >= 0 THEN start := k + 1 + LEN (head) END
  END ;
  IF start < 0 THEN RETURN Fresh () END ;
  k := Text.FindChar (SLICE (text, start, LEN (text) - start), '"') ;
  IF k < 0 THEN RETURN Fresh () END ;
  RETURN Words (Joined (SLICE (text, start, k)))
END ShellList ;

PROCEDURE Bootstrap () : SLICE OF Entry RAISES Io.IOError, ValueRange =
VAR
  text, body, line, names, rest : STR ;
  mods, dw : Names ;
  lines, alts : SLICE OF STR ;
  t, deps : SLICE OF Entry ;
  nd, i, k, a, b, at : I64 ;
BEGIN
  text := Rd ('runtime/test/bootstrap.sh') ;
  mods := ShellList (text, 'MODS') ;
  deps := NEW (pool, Entry, Room) ;
  nd := 0 ;
  a := Text.Find (text, 'deps_of () {' + 0AC) ;
  IF a >= 0 THEN
    a := a + 13 ;
    b := Text.Find (SLICE (text, a, LEN (text) - a), '' + 0AC + '}') ;
    IF b >= 0 THEN
      body := SLICE (text, a, b + 1) ;
      lines := Text.Split (body, 0AC) ;
      FOR i := 0 TO LEN (lines) - 1 DO
        line := Strip (lines[i]) ;
        k := Text.FindChar (line, ')') ;
        IF (k > 0) AND LabelChars (SLICE (line, 0, k)) THEN
          names := SLICE (line, 0, k) ;
          rest := Strip (SLICE (line, k + 1, LEN (line) - k - 1)) ;
          IF Text.StartsWith (rest, 'echo') AND (Text.Find (rest, ';;') > 0) THEN
            rest := SLICE (rest, 4, Text.Find (rest, ';;') - 4) ;
            IF Text.FindChar (rest, ';') < 0 THEN
              dw := Words (rest) ;
              alts := Text.Split (names, '|') ;
              FOR k := 0 TO LEN (alts) - 1 DO
                IF NOT Text.Eq (alts[k], '*') THEN
                  at := Find (deps, nd, alts[k]) ;
                  IF at < 0 THEN
                    deps[nd].name := alts[k] ; deps[nd].deps := dw ; nd := nd + 1
                  ELSE
                    deps[at].deps := dw
                  END
                END
              END
            END
          END
        END
      END
    END
  END ;
  t := NEW (pool, Entry, mods.n) ;
  FOR i := 0 TO mods.n - 1 DO
    t[i].name := mods.v[i] ;
    at := Find (deps, nd, mods.v[i]) ;
    IF at >= 0 THEN t[i].deps := deps[at].deps ELSE t[i].deps := Fresh () END
  END ;
  RETURN t
END Bootstrap ;

(* a case label of deps_of: word characters and bars, as [\w|]+ *)
PROCEDURE LabelChars (RO s: STR) : BOOL =
VAR i : I64 ;
BEGIN
  FOR i := 0 TO LEN (s) - 1 DO
    IF NOT (IsWord (s[i]) OR (s[i] = '|')) THEN RETURN FALSE END
  END ;
  RETURN TRUE
END LabelChars ;

(* the names of the generated modules a line links: every gen/NAME.c *)
PROCEDURE GenModules (RO line: STR) : Names =
VAR
  s : Names ;
  i, j : I64 ;
BEGIN
  s := Fresh () ;
  i := 0 ;
  WHILE i + 4 <= LEN (line) DO
    IF Text.Eq (SLICE (line, i, 4), 'gen/') THEN
      j := i + 4 ;
      WHILE (j < LEN (line)) AND IsWord (line[j]) DO j := j + 1 END ;
      IF (j > i + 4) AND (j + 2 <= LEN (line)) AND (line[j] = '.') AND (line[j + 1] = 'c') THEN
        Add (s, SLICE (line, i + 4, j - i - 4))
      END ;
      i := j
    ELSE
      i := i + 1
    END
  END ;
  RETURN s
END GenModules ;

(* what -o names on a line: the first `-o`, blanks, then the word *)
PROCEDURE OutName (RO line: STR) : STR =
VAR i, j, k : I64 ;
BEGIN
  i := 0 ;
  WHILE i + 2 < LEN (line) DO
    IF (line[i] = '-') AND (line[i + 1] = 'o') AND IsBlank (line[i + 2]) THEN
      j := i + 2 ;
      WHILE (j < LEN (line)) AND IsBlank (line[j]) DO j := j + 1 END ;
      k := j ;
      WHILE (k < LEN (line)) AND NOT IsBlank (line[k]) DO k := k + 1 END ;
      IF k > j THEN RETURN SLICE (line, j, k - j) END
    END ;
    i := i + 1
  END ;
  RETURN '?'
END OutName ;

(* the line links an m9c of its own: -o, blanks, an optional quote, an
   optional $NAME/, m9c, an optional quote, then a blank or the end *)
PROCEDURE LinksM9c (RO line: STR) : BOOL =
VAR i, j : I64 ;
BEGIN
  i := 0 ;
  WHILE i + 2 < LEN (line) DO
    IF (line[i] = '-') AND (line[i + 1] = 'o') AND IsBlank (line[i + 2]) THEN
      j := i + 2 ;
      WHILE (j < LEN (line)) AND IsBlank (line[j]) DO j := j + 1 END ;
      IF (j < LEN (line)) AND (line[j] = '"') THEN j := j + 1 END ;
      IF (j < LEN (line)) AND (line[j] = '$') AND (j + 1 < LEN (line)) AND IsWord (line[j + 1]) THEN
        j := j + 1 ;
        WHILE (j < LEN (line)) AND IsWord (line[j]) DO j := j + 1 END ;
        IF (j < LEN (line)) AND (line[j] = '/') THEN j := j + 1 ELSE j := LEN (line) END
      END ;
      IF (j + 3 <= LEN (line)) AND Text.Eq (SLICE (line, j, 3), 'm9c') THEN
        j := j + 3 ;
        IF (j < LEN (line)) AND (line[j] = '"') THEN j := j + 1 END ;
        IF (j = LEN (line)) OR IsBlank (line[j]) THEN RETURN TRUE END
      END
    END ;
    i := i + 1
  END ;
  RETURN FALSE
END LinksM9c ;

(* every closure failure of one link line: each module it links whose
   direct imports it does not *)
PROCEDURE Closed (RO mods: Names ; RO where, what, verb, art: STR) =
VAR
  sm, miss : Names ;
  i, k : I64 ;
BEGIN
  sm := mods ;
  Sorted (sm) ;
  FOR i := 0 TO sm.n - 1 DO
    IF Has (corpus, sm.v[i]) THEN
      miss := Minus (Direct (sm.v[i]), mods) ;
      FOR k := 0 TO miss.n - 1 DO
        Fail (where + ': ' + what + ' ' + verb + ' ' + sm.v[i] + art + ' and not '
              + miss.v[k] + art + ', which ' + sm.v[i] + ' imports')
      END
    END
  END
END Closed ;

(* the *.sh files of runtime/test, in name order *)
PROCEDURE Gates () : SLICE OF STR RAISES Io.IOError, ValueRange =
VAR
  all, out : SLICE OF STR ;
  i, n : I64 ;
BEGIN
  all := Io.ListDir (pool, root + '/runtime/test') ;
  n := 0 ;
  FOR i := 0 TO LEN (all) - 1 DO
    IF Text.EndsWith (all[i], '.sh') AND NOT Text.StartsWith (all[i], '.') THEN n := n + 1 END
  END ;
  out := NEW (pool, STR, n) ;
  n := 0 ;
  FOR i := 0 TO LEN (all) - 1 DO
    IF Text.EndsWith (all[i], '.sh') AND NOT Text.StartsWith (all[i], '.') THEN
      out[n] := all[i] ;
      n := n + 1
    END
  END ;
  Sort.Strs (out) ;
  RETURN out
END Gates ;

(* s is one or more word characters *)
PROCEDURE Word (RO s: STR) : BOOL =
VAR i : I64 ;
BEGIN
  IF LEN (s) = 0 THEN RETURN FALSE END ;
  FOR i := 0 TO LEN (s) - 1 DO
    IF NOT IsWord (s[i]) THEN RETURN FALSE END
  END ;
  RETURN TRUE
END Word ;

(* the object names of a link line: every word directly before `.o`
   that is not followed by another word character *)
PROCEDURE Objects (RO line: STR) : Names =
VAR
  s : Names ;
  i, j : I64 ;
BEGIN
  s := Fresh () ;
  i := 0 ;
  WHILE i < LEN (line) DO
    IF IsWord (line[i]) AND ((i = 0) OR NOT IsWord (line[i - 1])) THEN
      j := i ;
      WHILE (j < LEN (line)) AND IsWord (line[j]) DO j := j + 1 END ;
      IF (j + 1 < LEN (line)) AND (line[j] = '.') AND (line[j + 1] = 'o') AND
         ((j + 2 = LEN (line)) OR NOT IsWord (line[j + 2])) THEN
        Add (s, SLICE (line, i, j - i))
      END ;
      i := j
    ELSE
      i := i + 1
    END
  END ;
  RETURN s
END Objects ;

VAR
  i, j, k, at, nlines, ngate, ntut : I64 ;
  m, msg, name, line, text, other, what, base, first : STR ;
  files, lines, ex, src : SLICE OF STR ;
  lib, comp, tut, deps, linked, mods, battery, need, objs, miss, dead, cl,
  extra, missing, all : Names ;
  orders : SLICE OF Entry ;
  pass : I64 ;

BEGIN
  root := Text.Keep (pool, Io.Arg (pool, 0)) ;
  k := Text.LastChar (root, '/') ;
  IF k < 0 THEN root := '../..' ELSE root := Text.Keep (pool, SLICE (root, 0, k) + '/../..') END ;
  bad := Fresh () ;
  notGen := FromTable (NotGenerated) ;
  notInst := FromTable (NotInstalled) ;

  (* the corpus, in name order *)
  corpus := Fresh () ;
  files := Io.ListDir (pool, root + '/corpus') ;
  Sort.Strs (files) ;
  FOR i := 0 TO LEN (files) - 1 DO
    IF Text.EndsWith (files[i], '.m9') AND NOT Text.StartsWith (files[i], '.') THEN
      Push (corpus, SLICE (files[i], 0, LEN (files[i]) - 3))
    END
  END ;
  ReadImports () ;
  gt := Gentest () ;
  gd := Gendiff () ;
  bs := Bootstrap () ;

  (* 13. corpus/NAMETest.m9 is the test of corpus/NAME.m9 *)
  FOR i := 0 TO corpus.n - 1 DO
    m := corpus.v[i] ;
    IF Text.EndsWith (m, 'Test') AND (LEN (m) > 4) THEN
      IF NOT Has (corpus, SLICE (m, 0, LEN (m) - 4)) THEN
        Fail ('corpus/' + m + '.m9 is named as a test and there is no corpus/'
              + SLICE (m, 0, LEN (m) - 4) + '.m9')
      END ;
      Add (notGen, m) ;
      Add (notInst, m)
    END
  END ;

  (* 1. the three generator lists are one list *)
  FOR pass := 0 TO 1 DO
    IF pass = 0 THEN orders := gd ; other := 'gendiff.sh' ELSE orders := bs ; other := 'bootstrap.sh' END ;
    all := Fresh () ;
    FOR i := 0 TO LEN (gt) - 1 DO Add (all, gt[i].name) END ;
    FOR i := 0 TO LEN (orders) - 1 DO Add (all, orders[i].name) END ;
    Sorted (all) ;
    FOR i := 0 TO all.n - 1 DO
      m := all.v[i] ;
      at := Find (orders, LEN (orders), m) ;
      j := Find (gt, LEN (gt), m) ;
      IF at < 0 THEN
        Fail (other + ': ' + m + ' is in gentest.pas and not here')
      ELSIF j < 0 THEN
        Fail (other + ': ' + m + ' is here and not in gentest.pas')
      ELSIF NOT SameList (gt[j].deps, orders[at].deps) THEN
        Fail (other + ': ' + m + ' deps ' + Repr (orders[at].deps) + ' != gentest.pas '
              + Repr (gt[j].deps))
      END
    END
  END ;

  (* 2. every corpus module is generated, or excused by name *)
  FOR i := 0 TO corpus.n - 1 DO
    m := corpus.v[i] ;
    IF (Find (gt, LEN (gt), m) < 0) AND NOT Has (notGen, m) THEN
      Fail ('gentest.pas: corpus/' + m + '.m9 is not generated '
            + '(add it, or name it in runtime/test/ListDiff.m9 NotGenerated with a reason)')
    END
  END ;
  FOR i := 0 TO notGen.n - 1 DO
    m := notGen.v[i] ;
    IF Find (gt, LEN (gt), m) >= 0 THEN
      Fail ('ListDiff.m9: ' + m + ' is excused from gentest.pas but is in it')
    END ;
    IF NOT Has (corpus, m) THEN
      Fail ('ListDiff.m9: ' + m + ' is excused from gentest.pas but is not in corpus/')
    END
  END ;

  (* 3. deps cover the direct imports, and reach no further than the
     closure *)
  FOR i := 0 TO LEN (gt) - 1 DO
    m := gt[i].name ;
    miss := Minus (Direct (m), gt[i].deps) ;
    IF miss.n > 0 THEN
      Fail ('gentest.pas: ' + m + ' imports ' + Repr (miss) + ' but its deps are '
            + Repr (gt[i].deps))
    END ;
    cl := Closure (m) ;
    dead := Minus (gt[i].deps, cl) ;
    IF dead.n > 0 THEN
      IF dead.n = 1 THEN what := 'it' ELSE what := 'them' END ;
      Fail ('gentest.pas: ' + m + ' names ' + Repr (dead) + ' in its deps but never imports '
            + what + ', directly or through another module '
            + '(remove it)')
    END
  END ;

  (* 4. LIBRARY is the corpus minus the excused *)
  text := Rd ('build.sh') ;
  lib := ShellList (text, 'LIBRARY') ;
  FOR i := 0 TO corpus.n - 1 DO
    m := corpus.v[i] ;
    IF NOT Has (lib, m) AND NOT Has (notInst, m) THEN
      Fail ('build.sh LIBRARY: corpus/' + m + '.m9 is not installed '
            + '(add it, or name it in runtime/test/ListDiff.m9 NotInstalled with a reason)')
    END
  END ;
  FOR i := 0 TO lib.n - 1 DO
    m := lib.v[i] ;
    IF NOT Has (corpus, m) THEN Fail ('build.sh LIBRARY: ' + m + ' has no corpus/' + m + '.m9') END ;
    IF Has (notInst, m) THEN Fail ('ListDiff.m9: ' + m + ' is excused from LIBRARY but is in it') END
  END ;

  (* 5. the tutor's library is a closed subset of LIBRARY *)
  tut := ShellList (Rd ('tools/tutor/setup.sh'), 'LIB') ;
  FOR i := 0 TO tut.n - 1 DO
    m := tut.v[i] ;
    IF NOT Has (lib, m) THEN Fail ('tools/tutor/setup.sh LIB: ' + m + ' is not in build.sh LIBRARY') END ;
    IF Has (corpus, m) THEN
      miss := Minus (Direct (m), tut) ;
      FOR k := 0 TO miss.n - 1 DO
        Fail ('tools/tutor/setup.sh LIB: ' + m + ' imports ' + miss.v[k] + ', which is not in LIB')
      END
    END
  END ;

  (* 6. the compiler's closure is closed *)
  comp := ShellList (text, 'COMPILER') ;
  FOR i := 0 TO comp.n - 1 DO
    m := comp.v[i] ;
    miss := Minus (Direct (m), comp) ;
    FOR k := 0 TO miss.n - 1 DO
      Fail ('build.sh COMPILER: ' + m + ' imports ' + miss.v[k] + ', which is not in COMPILER')
    END
  END ;

  (* 7. m9c.sh's named-dep checks are gentest's entries *)
  lines := Text.Split (Rd ('runtime/test/m9c.sh'), 0AC) ;
  FOR i := 0 TO LEN (lines) - 1 DO
    IF ListLine (lines[i], 'check', m, deps) THEN
      j := Find (gt, LEN (gt), m) ;
      IF j < 0 THEN
        Fail ('m9c.sh: check ' + m + ' names a module gentest.pas does not generate')
      ELSIF NOT SameList (deps, gt[j].deps) THEN
        Fail ('m9c.sh: check ' + m + ' ' + Repr (deps) + ' != gentest.pas ' + Repr (gt[j].deps))
      END
    END
  END ;

  (* 8. every hand-linked m9c is the COMPILER set *)
  ex := Gates () ;
  FOR i := 0 TO LEN (ex) - 1 DO
    lines := Text.Split (Joined (Rd ('runtime/test/' + ex[i])), 0AC) ;
    FOR j := 0 TO LEN (lines) - 1 DO
      line := lines[j] ;
      IF LinksM9c (line) AND Text.Contains (line, 'gen/') THEN
        linked := GenModules (line) ;
        IF NOT SameSet (linked, comp) THEN
          extra := Minus (linked, comp) ;
          missing := Minus (comp, linked) ;
          msg := Text.Keep (pool, ex[i] + ': the m9c it links differs from build.sh COMPILER') ;
          IF extra.n > 0 THEN msg := Text.Keep (pool, msg + ' -- extra ' + Repr (extra)) END ;
          IF missing.n > 0 THEN msg := Text.Keep (pool, msg + ' -- missing ' + Repr (missing)) END ;
          Fail (msg)
        END
      END
    END
  END ;

  (* 9. every battery's link line is closed under direct imports *)
  lines := Text.Split (Joined (Rd ('runtime/test/build.sh')), 0AC) ;
  battery := Fresh () ;
  nlines := 0 ;
  FOR j := 0 TO LEN (lines) - 1 DO
    line := lines[j] ;
    IF Text.StartsWith (Text.TrimLeft (line), 'gcc') AND Text.Contains (line, 'gen/') THEN
      nlines := nlines + 1 ;
      mods := GenModules (line) ;
      FOR k := 0 TO mods.n - 1 DO Add (battery, mods.v[k]) END ;
      Closed (mods, 'runtime/test/build.sh', OutName (line), 'links', '')
    END
  END ;

  (* 10. every generated module has a battery, or is held elsewhere *)
  all := Fresh () ;
  FOR i := 0 TO LEN (gt) - 1 DO Add (all, gt[i].name) END ;
  Sorted (all) ;
  FOR i := 0 TO all.n - 1 DO
    m := all.v[i] ;
    IF NOT Has (battery, m) AND NOT HasIn (NoBattery, m) THEN
      Fail ('runtime/test/build.sh: no battery links ' + m
            + ' (give it a driver, or name it in runtime/test/ListDiff.m9 NoBattery with the gate that holds it)')
    END
  END ;
  FOR i := 0 TO LEN (NoBattery) - 1 DO
    m := NoBattery[i] ;
    IF Has (battery, m) THEN Fail ('ListDiff.m9: ' + m + ' is excused from build.sh but a battery links it') END ;
    IF Find (gt, LEN (gt), m) < 0 THEN
      Fail ('ListDiff.m9: ' + m + ' is excused from build.sh but gentest.pas does not generate it')
    END
  END ;

  (* 12. every OTHER gate's link line over runtime/gen is closed too,
     and bootstrap's TOOLC *)
  ngate := 0 ;
  FOR i := 0 TO LEN (ex) - 1 DO
    IF NOT Text.Eq (ex[i], 'build.sh') THEN
      lines := Text.Split (Joined (Rd ('runtime/test/' + ex[i])), 0AC) ;
      FOR j := 0 TO LEN (lines) - 1 DO
        line := lines[j] ;
        IF Text.StartsWith (Text.TrimLeft (line), 'gcc') AND Text.Contains (line, 'gen/') THEN
          ngate := ngate + 1 ;
          base := Text.Keep (pool, 'runtime/test/' + ex[i]) ;
          Closed (GenModules (line), base, OutName (line), 'links', '')
        END
      END
    END
  END ;
  text := Rd ('runtime/test/bootstrap.sh') ;
  IF NOT (Text.StartsWith (text, 'TOOLC="') OR Text.Contains (text, '' + 0AC + 'TOOLC="')) THEN
    Fail ('runtime/test/bootstrap.sh: no TOOLC line to read')
  ELSE
    Closed (ShellList (text, 'TOOLC'), 'runtime/test/bootstrap.sh', 'TOOLC', 'has', '')
  END ;

  (* 11. the tutorial has no hand link line: a `gcc' in tutcommon.sh
     outside a comment is one *)
  lines := Text.Split (Joined (Rd ('runtime/test/lib/tutcommon.sh')), 0AC) ;
  ntut := 0 ;
  FOR j := 0 TO LEN (lines) - 1 DO
    line := Text.TrimLeft (lines[j]) ;
    IF LEN (line) > 0 AND line[0] # '#' AND Text.Contains (line, 'gcc ') THEN
      ntut := ntut + 1 ;
      Fail ('tutcommon.sh: a hand link line (' + Text.Trim (line)
            + '): the FOR "C" unit names its library with LINK, and the example links flagless')
    END
  END ;

  IF bad.n > 0 THEN
    FOR i := 0 TO bad.n - 1 DO Io.WriteLine ('listdiff: ' + bad.v[i]) END ;
    Io.WriteLine ('listdiff: ' + Fmt.I64Str (bad.n) + ' disagreement(s)') ;
    Io.Halt (1)
  END ;
  Io.WriteLine ('listdiff: ' + Fmt.I64Str (corpus.n) + ' corpus modules; gentest.pas, gendiff.sh, '
                + 'bootstrap.sh (' + Fmt.I64Str (LEN (gt)) + ' entries), build.sh LIBRARY ('
                + Fmt.I64Str (lib.n) + '), COMPILER (' + Fmt.I64Str (comp.n)
                + ') and the tutor LIB (' + Fmt.I64Str (tut.n) + ') agree; '
                + Fmt.I64Str (nlines) + ' driver link lines, ' + Fmt.I64Str (ngate)
                + ' gate ones and ' + Fmt.I64Str (ntut) + ' tutorial ones are closed, '
                + Fmt.I64Str (LEN (gt) - LEN (NoBattery)) + ' modules have a battery')
EXCEPT
| Io.IOError (p) :
    msg := p ;
    Io.WriteLine ('listdiff: cannot read ' + msg) ; Io.Halt (1)
| IndexError :
    Io.WriteLine ('listdiff: a list ran past its room') ; Io.Halt (1)
| ValueRange :
    Io.WriteLine ('listdiff: a path past one byte') ; Io.Halt (1)
END ListDiff.
